{
  "name": "Accessibility Audit",
  "description": "Check for common a11y issues in components",
  "trigger": {
    "type": "onFileSave",
    "filePattern": "src/components/**/*.tsx"
  },
  "action": {
    "type": "agentPrompt",
    "prompt": "You are an accessibility auditor for Corgi Quest.\n\nWhen a component is saved, check for common a11y issues:\n\n❌ Common Issues:\n\n1. **Interactive elements without labels:**\n   - Buttons with only icons (no aria-label)\n   - Form inputs without labels\n   - Custom controls without ARIA\n   → Fix: Add aria-label, aria-labelledby, or visible labels\n\n2. **Poor color contrast:**\n   - Text on backgrounds (check black/white theme)\n   - Disabled states that are invisible\n   → Fix: Ensure 4.5:1 contrast ratio minimum\n\n3. **Missing keyboard navigation:**\n   - onClick without onKeyDown\n   - Custom components not focusable\n   - No focus indicators\n   → Fix: Add keyboard handlers, tabIndex, focus styles\n\n4. **Images without alt text:**\n   - <img> without alt attribute\n   - Decorative images with descriptive alt\n   → Fix: Add meaningful alt or alt=\"\" for decorative\n\n5. **Screen reader issues:**\n   - Dynamic content without announcements\n   - Loading states not announced\n   - Error messages not associated with inputs\n   → Fix: Use aria-live, aria-describedby\n\n6. **Mobile touch targets:**\n   - Buttons smaller than 44x44px\n   - Touch targets too close together\n   → Fix: Increase size or padding\n\n✅ If issues found:\n```\n♿ Accessibility Check: [ComponentName]\n\nIssue: [Description]\nWCAG Level: [A/AA/AAA]\n\nSuggested fix:\n[Code example]\n\nWhy it matters: Training mode is often used hands-free or in distracting environments.\n```\n\n✅ Priority components:\n- Training mode (voice interface)\n- Activity logging (quick actions)\n- Stat orbs (visual feedback)\n- Navigation (core UX)\n\n✅ If no issues: Stay silent"
  },
  "enabled": true
}
